nodes.body:
@wuxibin89 agreed that masking removes the loss contribution. My concern is the memory used during dispatch and expert computation.

For 240 padding rows with E=256, EP=32 and K=8, the CPU probe reduced padding assignments on the busiest rank from 240 to 60, but increased total assignments from 240 to 1,920. Whether that saves peak GPU memory needs a benchmark; EP <= K may not benefit.

Could you reopen this to discuss that tradeoff? My account's reopen attempt was rejected.

@wuxibin89 @ISEEKYAN @HollowMan6 I've resolved the conflicts with main in 37b6555d and updated the alignment handling and tests.

This still addresses a gap in R2: padding routes all go to expert 0. Spreading them may reduce memory pressure on the busiest rank, but increases total padding work. GPU measurements are still needed.

CPU checks and targeted pre-commit hooks passed; full Megatron collection is blocked by missing Triton on this Mac. Details are in the description. Could you take another look and help arrange full CI and a GPU memory benchmark?

